      "artist": "iom_mark from Douglas, Isle of Man",
      "description": "As tourist numbers dwindled Summerland was built and became Europes largest indoor entertainment facility long before Butlins and Center Parcs were thought up.\nA fire in 1973 resulted in tradgey with over 50 deaths. Large open areas, locked doors and flamable materials used during construction aided the spread of the fire and toxic fumes.\nAlthough rebuilding took place it eventually closed in the late 1990s, demolition folled only to be halted when it was found that it was supporting the surrounding rockface and cliffs. Homeowners above the cliff expressed concerns.\n\nThis photo from October 2006 shows the skeletal remains waiting to close the book on this sad history.",
